les, search these specific websites When a scientific question is asked, go to Science, Nature, go to this and that So you will input this specific command within the Artificial Intelligence Also, where you direct the Artificial Intelligence to go, the responses of the Artificial Intelligence Will reflect wherever it is collecting data from So you need to understand this is just a programme, and that programme is collecting information, Depending on the person who programmed it, where it's going to collect the information from", "Now keep in mind, the people who are designing these programmes are not Muslims They're non-Muslims, and they are Western people, and they have their own agendas You know, you look at DeepSeek, whether it's used by the Chinese, Or you look at Grok being used by– each of these people have their own agendas And therefore, whatever that Artificial Intelligence is going to say, and answer you, and reflect, Most of the time is going to be based on the views that these people hold, And the agendas that they're trying to accomplish So, the problem is when people don't understand the biases within these programmes, And that leads to huge issues Like for example, recently, come across like many people who are like experiencing doubts, some of them have become hyper sceptics Why?", "Because they go to ChatGPT, like the Quran says: (ask the people of knowledge if you don’t know) (anNahl16:43) They think it's: go ask ChatGPT if you don't know! So they go to Sheikh ChatGPT, or Sheikh Grok, or whatever, and they go ask him questions And then they get confused Why are they getting confused? Because that Artificial Intelligence programme is either collecting information from Reddit, or from.. whatever articles out there online in the English language And then it's responding to the questions, and most of the people commenting and making posts in these websites are non-Muslims: people who hate Islam, misrepresent Islam, and put incorrect information So when